WEBVTT

00:00:02.795 --> 00:00:05.590
Well, why don't you call some more people
to barge in and help?

00:00:05.673 --> 00:00:07.008
[all] Ooh!

00:00:07.091 --> 00:00:08.634
[phone rings]

00:00:09.177 --> 00:00:11.971
[Snake] Welcome, friend,
fo Mr. Snake's voice mall.

00:00:12.055 --> 00:00:13.556
Today's advice for the soul:

00:00:13.639 --> 00:00:16.559
We must stop concentrating
on our differences

00:00:16.642 --> 00:00:19.270
and look for what we have in common.

00:00:19.354 --> 00:00:20.938
-Namaste.
-[groans]

00:00:21.022 --> 00:00:23.566
-Bye!
-[beeps]

00:00:23.649 --> 00:00:25.026
Is he possessed?

00:00:25.109 --> 00:00:26.611
Ugh, don't even get me started.

00:00:26.694 --> 00:00:29.072
I mean, one day he's going to yoga,
he's doing pottery.

00:00:29.155 --> 00:00:31.324
I mean, who does pottery,
the cast of Ghost?

00:00:31.407 --> 00:00:33.117
-Guys, guys, guys. Hold on.
-[all] Huh?

00:00:33.201 --> 00:00:34.202
What did he say again?

00:00:34.285 --> 00:00:36.579
"Look for what we have in common."

00:00:37.830 --> 00:00:39.665
Look. It's not about the artifacts.

00:00:39.749 --> 00:00:41.542
It's about what they have in common.

00:00:41.626 --> 00:00:44.379
They're all made from a rare metal
called MacGuffinite.

00:00:44.462 --> 00:00:45.463
[Tarantula] Of course.

00:00:45.546 --> 00:00:47.173
Uh, MacGuff-a-what now?

00:00:47.256 --> 00:00:49.050
Uh, sounds kind of made up.

00:00:49.133 --> 00:00:51.469
So does the word "gold"
if you didn't know it was real.

00:00:51.552 --> 00:00:52.553
Say "gold."

00:00:53.137 --> 00:00:56.516
-Gold. Gold. Gold!
-Gold, gold, gold.

00:00:56.599 --> 00:00:58.017
That does sound made up!

00:00:58.101 --> 00:01:01.020
Now I can't stop thinking
how it sounds weird. Gold.

00:01:01.104 --> 00:01:03.022
So now that we know
what the Bandit is after...

00:01:03.106 --> 00:01:06.150
We can figure out
where he's gonna strike next.

00:01:06.234 --> 00:01:08.736
There you go. That's the chief I know.

00:01:09.237 --> 00:01:11.155
Hmm. You grinding
your own beans these days?

00:01:12.198 --> 00:01:13.950
It's commissioner.

00:01:14.033 --> 00:01:15.618
Now get out of my office.

00:01:16.953 --> 00:01:18.287
["Shake Your Groove Thing" playing]

00:01:18.371 --> 00:01:20.957
> Shake your groove thing
Shake your groove thing »

00:01:21.040 --> 00:01:22.041
<i>> Yeah, yeah »</i>

00:01:22.125 --> 00:01:25.670
Woo! Next thing you know,
we're on TV getting medals.

00:01:25.753 --> 00:01:27.463
Naming streets after us.

00:01:27.547 --> 00:01:29.507
-Piranha Street, baby.
-[chuckles]

00:01:29.590 --> 00:01:30.591
Hey, listen to this.

00:01:30.675 --> 00:01:34.512
Translated into English, the word
"MacGuffinite" means "a small MacGuffin."

00:01:34.595 --> 00:01:35.596
Cute.

00:01:35.680 --> 00:01:38.975
Okay. Not super helpful,
but, uh, what else you got?

00:01:39.058 --> 00:01:41.394
[Tarantula] The most famous
MacGuffinite object is

00:01:41.477 --> 00:01:44.397
-The Belt of Guatelamango.
-[Shark gasps]

00:01:44.480 --> 00:01:46.524
Did you say The Belt of Guatelamango?

00:01:46.607 --> 00:01:47.859
You heard of that?

00:01:47.942 --> 00:01:50.194
Heard of it?
It's the championship trophy

00:01:50.278 --> 00:01:52.530
for the Lords of Lucha tournament.

00:01:53.156 --> 00:01:55.074
Wait, isn't that where
Snake is going tonight?

00:01:55.158 --> 00:01:56.325
That's right.

00:01:56.409 --> 00:01:59.162
Can you imagine him
at a wrestling match?

00:01:59.245 --> 00:02:00.371
He hates crowds.

00:02:00.455 --> 00:02:01.456
And loud music.

00:02:01.539 --> 00:02:03.207
And flamboyant costumes.

00:02:03.291 --> 00:02:05.293
And things that make life worthwhile.

00:02:05.376 --> 00:02:07.044
[all laughing]

00:02:12.258 --> 00:02:13.551
-Oh, no.
-[brakes squeal]

00:02:13.634 --> 00:02:14.927
-[thuds] Ow!
-[music ends]

00:02:15.011 --> 00:02:16.554
[shouts]

00:02:18.931 --> 00:02:20.057
It's Snake.

00:02:20.141 --> 00:02:21.517
[mysterious music plays]

00:02:21.601 --> 00:02:22.894
It's all right here.

00:02:22.977 --> 00:02:26.564
Happy hour. Pottery. Yoga.

00:02:26.647 --> 00:02:28.858
All the same times
as the Bandit's robberies.

00:02:28.941 --> 00:02:30.735
He's been lying to us
this whole time.

00:02:30.818 --> 00:02:32.778
Ooh, he's such a little snake.

00:02:32.862 --> 00:02:34.614
That's why he's so happy.

00:02:34.697 --> 00:02:36.991
-Oh.
-Vinyasa my butt.

00:02:37.074 --> 00:02:39.368
If he gets caught,
he's going back to prison.

00:02:39.452 --> 00:02:42.121
We gotta find him before
Police Chief cracks the case.

00:02:42.205 --> 00:02:43.915
-[phone rings]
-Uh-oh.

00:02:45.666 --> 00:02:47.460
-[line chimes]
-Hello?

00:02:47.543 --> 00:02:48.586
[laughing]

00:02:48.669 --> 00:02:52.548
Guess who has two thumbs,
bangs and cracked the case?

00:02:52.632 --> 00:02:54.008
This gal!

00:02:54.091 --> 00:02:55.259
Oh, really?

00:02:55.343 --> 00:02:58.971
It's going down tonight at
the Lords of Lucha tournament.

00:02:59.055 --> 00:03:00.473
-[all gasp]
-I am going to catch

00:03:00.556 --> 00:03:02.725
-that Bandit red-handed.
-Ah!

00:03:02.808 --> 00:03:06.312
...well done, Wolf. Well done.
You have exceeded my expect--

00:03:06.395 --> 00:03:07.688
[phone clatters in distance]

00:03:08.231 --> 00:03:09.941
Bro, that was our only phone!

00:03:10.024 --> 00:03:11.359
What the thorax?

00:03:11.442 --> 00:03:12.735
I don't know. I panicked.

00:03:13.945 --> 00:03:15.530
Guys, there's only one play here.

00:03:15.613 --> 00:03:16.614
Find our friend and--

00:03:16.697 --> 00:03:22.245
Tear him apart limb by limb
until all he can remember is pain!

00:03:22.328 --> 00:03:23.496
[panting]

00:03:23.579 --> 00:03:25.623
Wow, okay.
I was gonna say save him,

00:03:25.706 --> 00:03:27.708
but, sure, if there's time,
we can do the limb thing.

00:03:27.792 --> 00:03:29.043
[groans]

00:03:29.293 --> 00:03:31.754
-[engine sputtering]
-[explosion]

00:03:33.464 --> 00:03:34.590
[Spanish rock music plays]

00:03:34.674 --> 00:03:36.133
[car alarm blares]

00:03:37.343 --> 00:03:41.597
[announcer] Ladies and gentlemen,
put your hands together

00:03:41.681 --> 00:03:45.893
for the current reigning world champion,

00:03:45.977 --> 00:03:50.690
Handsome Jorge!

00:03:50.773 --> 00:03:52.733
-Ah, yes! Mwah! Mwah!
-[crowd cheers]

00:03:53.985 --> 00:03:57.238
[announcer] Face of an angel.
Punch of el Diablo.

00:04:08.583 --> 00:04:09.959
Snake!

00:04:10.042 --> 00:04:11.669
-[growls]
-I'm gonna kill you!

00:04:19.218 --> 00:04:20.720
[engines revving]

00:04:22.221 --> 00:04:23.264
Wow.

00:04:29.478 --> 00:04:32.273
And Mama said I'd never get to heaven.

00:04:33.399 --> 00:04:34.775
Look at me now, Mama!

00:04:36.319 --> 00:04:37.361
[Piranha chuckles]

00:04:37.445 --> 00:04:40.239
I'm gonna need a lot of mustard.

00:04:40.323 --> 00:04:42.158
[Shark] Piranha, check it out.

00:04:42.241 --> 00:04:44.201
One in your size and one in my size!

00:04:44.285 --> 00:04:45.661
Guys, we can shop later.

00:04:45.745 --> 00:04:47.913
Right now, we need to find Snake.
Let's go. Come on.

00:04:47.997 --> 00:04:49.790
Ooh, right, right, right.
It's just so much!

00:04:49.874 --> 00:04:51.626
Now, listen. He could be anywhere.

00:04:51.709 --> 00:04:52.877
Webs, search the upper deck.

00:04:52.960 --> 00:04:53.961
I'll look ringside.

00:04:54.045 --> 00:04:55.588
-You two--
-Guys!

00:04:55.671 --> 00:04:58.674
I can't believe you came all this way
just to see me arrest the Bandit--

00:04:58.758 --> 00:04:59.759
Ah!

00:05:00.760 --> 00:05:01.927
What? What was that?

00:05:02.011 --> 00:05:04.639
I don't know. I panicked, okay?
I'm a panicker.

00:05:04.722 --> 00:05:06.307
[Luggins snoring]

00:05:11.812 --> 00:05:12.855
Okay, no more panicking.

00:05:12.938 --> 00:05:14.273
Webs, search the upper deck.

00:05:14.357 --> 00:05:15.608
You two, backstage.

00:05:15.691 --> 00:05:18.527
Remember, we're dealing
with a master of deception

00:05:18.611 --> 00:05:20.946
who can move like water
and vanish like smoke.

00:05:21.030 --> 00:05:22.907
-He could be anywhere--
-There he is.

00:05:24.909 --> 00:05:26.202
-[Wolf] Snake!
-Huh?

00:05:26.285 --> 00:05:28.704
-[growling]
-[screaming]

00:05:28.788 --> 00:05:29.955
We know everything!

00:05:30.039 --> 00:05:31.415
What? How did you find out?

00:05:31.499 --> 00:05:32.875
-[growls]
-Ow!

00:05:35.920 --> 00:05:37.380
[Susan] Snakey Cakes?

00:05:37.463 --> 00:05:38.589
-Uh...
-Huh?

00:05:38.673 --> 00:05:39.799
[Snake groans]

00:05:40.549 --> 00:05:41.717
Uh... [chuckles]

00:05:41.801 --> 00:05:45.554
If I knew you were expecting friends,
I would have gotten more nachos.

00:05:45.638 --> 00:05:47.348
Because, well, I know
you don't like to share.

00:05:47.431 --> 00:05:48.432
That's true.

00:05:48.516 --> 00:05:50.351
Unless it's kisses.

00:05:50.434 --> 00:05:53.562
Then he likes to share,
don't you, Snakey Wakey?

00:05:54.271 --> 00:05:55.272
[chuckles]

